Meghadūta

with the commentaries of

Vallabhadeva, Dakṣiṇavartanātha, Mallinātha and Sumativijaya.

Input by Roger Vogt in 2009

with the kind and benevolent support of Ganeśa and Sarasvatī,

to whose lotos feet I bow, in order to ward off the evil daemon,

who constantly causes us to commit typing errors.

Anusvāra appears only before semivowels, sibilants and visarga.

Thus: saṃyoga, kiṃsvit, evaṃvidha but sañjñā, kiñcit kathambhūta
etc.

Wherever I thought it be necessary for a better understanding of the text
I have added or omitted Daṇḍas.

